---
import FeaturedLessons from '../components/FeaturedLessons.astro';
import LearningRoutes from '../components/LearningRoutes.astro';
import BookLayout from '../layouts/BookLayout.astro';

import modelSnapshot from '../data/commercial-model-snapshot.json';
import { chapters } from '../data/chapters.js';
import { servingGuide } from '../data/site.js';
import { withBasePath, withPagePath } from '../utils/paths.js';
---

<BookLayout title="Home" lang="en">
  <h1>Foundation Model Engineering</h1>
  <p>A free English and Korean textbook on training, serving, and evaluating foundation models, with browser experiments and CPU PyTorch labs.</p>

  <FeaturedLessons lang="en" />

  <h2>Model selection and cost</h2>
  <p>The November 24 comparison covers <a href={withPagePath('/chapter-17/commercial-model-benchmarks')}>{modelSnapshot.models.length} model profiles</a>. Check how to access <a href={withPagePath('/chapter-17/commercial-model-benchmarks') + '#model-glm-54'}>GLM-5.4</a>, find the context limit in the public <a href={withPagePath('/chapter-17/commercial-model-benchmarks') + '#model-ling-32-air'}>Ling-3.2-air checkpoint</a>, or calculate what one extra input token can do to the <a href={withPagePath('/chapter-17/commercial-model-benchmarks') + '#long-context-cost'}>GPT-6.2 Astra and Sol bill</a>. <a href={withPagePath('/chapter-11/audio-and-speech-integration')}>Speech</a>, <a href={withPagePath('/chapter-11/image-diffusion-models')}>image</a> and <a href={withPagePath('/chapter-11/commercial-video-models')}>video models</a> have their own evaluation chapters.</p>

  <LearningRoutes lang="en" />

  <h2>Train a small decoder on a CPU</h2>
  <p>How much of a repeating sequence can a decoder copy when it loses access to earlier tokens? Inspect <a href={withPagePath('/chapter-7/tiny-decoder-lab') + '#decoder-copy-trace'}>the predictions token by token</a>, then <a href="https://colab.research.google.com/github/sungeuns/foundation-model-engineering/blob/main/public/labs/tiny-decoder-lab.ipynb">run the experiment in Colab</a> or <a href={withBasePath('/labs/tiny-decoder-lab.ipynb')} download="tiny-decoder-lab.ipynb">download the Jupyter notebook</a>. The code generates its own data. Running it on Colab requires a Google sign-in.</p>

  <h2>About the book</h2>
  <p>For offline reading, <a href={servingGuide.downloads.en} type="application/epub+zip">download the three-lesson serving guide (EPUB)</a>. It covers KV memory, request scheduling and streaming latency.</p>
  <p>Seongeun So develops this independent textbook with AI assistance. Browse <a href="#book-contents">all {chapters.reduce((n, chapter) => n + chapter.subs.length, 0)} lessons</a> or <a href="https://github.com/sungeuns/foundation-model-engineering">bookmark the repository on GitHub</a>. If an example behaves differently from the explanation, <a href="https://github.com/sungeuns/foundation-model-engineering/issues/new/choose">report the chapter and the inputs that reproduce it</a>.</p>
  <p class="last-update">Last update <time datetime="2026-11-25">2026-11-25</time></p>

  <h2 id="book-contents">Table of Contents</h2>
  <div class="toc">
    {chapters.map(ch => (
      <div class="toc-chapter">
        <h3>{ch.title.en}</h3>
        <ul>
          {ch.subs.map(sub => (
            <li><a href={withPagePath(sub.path)}>{sub.title.en}</a></li>
          ))}
        </ul>
      </div>
    ))}
  </div>

</BookLayout>

<style>
  .last-update { color: var(--secondary-color); font-size: .9rem; }
  .toc {
    margin-top: 2rem;
  }
  .toc-chapter {
    margin-bottom: 1.5rem;
  }
  .toc h3 {
    font-size: 1.3rem;
    margin-bottom: 0.5rem;
    color: #111;
  }
  .toc ul {
    list-style: none;
    padding-left: 1rem;
  }
  .toc li {
    margin-bottom: 0.25rem;
  }
  .toc a {
    text-decoration: none;
    color: var(--accent-color);
  }
  .toc a:hover {
    text-decoration: underline;
  }
</style>
